## Context

Child of 1654 (tracker). Keeps the 29 September consultation: two rounds, a third only if the second brings admissible works. Rerun conditions: interrupted query, missed sentinel, external reference without decision, incomplete summary. Seeds keep uncertain works and sentinel routes; the fully graded set alone is not the discovery universe.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Round two run with counts (references and citations, duplicates, new works), its frontier chosen from scored works under the calibrated cut (ticket 2060).
- [ ] New works delivered under the intake contract, merged, and scored by the redesign; venue data refreshed; counts reconciled before the round's yield is measured.
- [ ] Third round triggered or dropped, with the measurement that decides it.
- [ ] Unresolved references and the evidence for stopping recorded, including any further chaining the protocol's closure rule requires; interrupted queries, missed sentinels and undecided external references do not support a saturation claim.
